 "summary": "Adds validation invariants and test coverage ensuring that block reorganizations do not evict existing mempool transactions or reject re-added transactions on mempool policy. It adds two Assume checks to Chainstate::MaybeUpdateMempoolForReorg, adds a functional test covering TRUC sibling eviction on reorg, and updates the tx_pool fuzz harness to test reorg handling against transactions rejected by the mempool.",
 "problem": "Transactions resurrected from disconnected blocks must bypass standard mempool policy checks like TRUC sibling limits and package constraints. If policy rules are mistakenly applied during a reorg, transactions can be dropped or evicted, stranding descendant transactions with missing inputs as occurred in CVE-2025-62861.",
 "evidence": [
  "Commit d223122202 notes this catches regressions of the CVE-2025-62861 fix (#33504), where an evicted TRUC child's descendant was left spending a missing output"
 ],
