 "card": "Adds validation invariants, functional tests, and fuzz harness improvements to ensure transactions re-added during block reorganizations never evict mempool transactions or get rejected on policy. This prevents regressions of CVE-2025-62861 (fixed in merged PR #33504), where re-evaluating TRUC policy during a reorg evicted a child transaction and left its descendant spending a nonexistent output. The changes add Assume checks in MaybeUpdateMempoolForReorg, a functional test in mempool_truc.py, and realistic reorg path execution in the tx_pool fuzzer. No dependencies are stated.",
